# Whats on Brisbane

## Africa Day Festival May 31st 2015

Another awesome event happening very soon and we hope to make it along this year! Here is the event info and the [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/events/1718233085070101/) event link where you can find out this and more info: _"Africa Day Festival is our signature event on the lawns of African House_ _Come experience rich and colourful African cultures at the Africa Day Festival_ _The festival showcases African art, clothing, dance, music and food, with activities for kids. There are also workshops on African drumming and many more._ _Festival goers can enjoy lunch at the food marquees, browse the many stalls with African inspired items. Then stay for the fantastic traditional performances on stage before having a drink at our bar to close out the day._ _This is an opportunity to bring together African communities to celebrate our cultures with each other and the rest of the community. Everyone is welcome at this free event – we want to see many colourful faces on the day._ _Over 7,000 people attend the festival, now in its seventh year. The festival has great participation from across African communities, businesses and performers._ _The festival is supported by the Queensland Government and Brisbane City Council as major sponsors."_ [Facebook event](https://www.facebook.com/events/1718233085070101/)
